Chapter: DtlsFragmentedFlightTest
  cites Net chapter DtlsEndpoint
  cites Encode chapter TlsCert
  cites Foreword chapter Tls
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A server whose certificate chain does not fit one datagram must still be
 reachable. The discriminating arm is max-record: before send-side
 fragmentation the flight went out as one record of about 1400 bytes, which
 a 1280-byte IPv6 path drops entirely, and every other arm here still
 passed because both endpoints were in the same process and no path was
 ever involved. Comparing the biggest emitted record against
 dtls-ep-mtu is the only arm that can tell the two apart.

